  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes of each lottery and considers differences between outcomes as negligible. This implies that outcomes such as 2500, 2400, and 0 are treated as sufficiently similar in value to be considered practically equivalent. Under this assumption, the reason directs the decision-maker to prefer the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. In this context, a 'favorable outcome' would be any non-zero outcome. For Lottery A, the probability of a favorable outcome (2400 Euros) is 100%. For Lottery B, the probability of a favorable outcome (either 2500 or 2400 Euros) is 99% (33% + 66%). Thus, Lottery A has a higher probability of a favorable outcome (100% vs. 99%).",
